439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 156 0 R
/T (\(a\) All result disputes must be submitted in writing to the Director of Studies and Quality Assurance Office within  Fourteen \(14\) calendar days from the official date of release of the results in question. Disputes submitted after  this window will not be entertained under any circumstances.  \(b\) The written dispute must clearly state: the module and assessment concerned, the result received, the specific  grounds for the dispute, and any supporting evidence the student wishes to be considered.  \(c\) The Director of Studies and Quality Assurance Office will acknowledge receipt of the dispute within five \(5\)  working days and will aim to resolve the matter within twenty-one \(21\) working days from the date of  acknowledgement.  \(d\) Where a re-marking or re-evaluation is requested and granted, the outcome of the re-assessment shall be  final and binding. A re-mark may result in the grade being upheld, increased, or decreased. \(e\) Disputes relating to administrative processing errors \(e.g. data entry mistakes\) will be resolved within five \(5\)  working days of submission.  \(f\) The Academy's determination of all academic disputes shall be final, subject only to any rights of appeal  provided under applicable Ugandan law. )
/E (\(a\) All result disputes must be submitted in writing to the Director of Studies and Quality Assurance Office within  Fourteen \(14\) calendar days from the official date of release of the results in question. Disputes submitted after  this window will not be entertained under any circumstances.  \(b\) The written dispute must clearly state: the module and assessment concerned, the result received, the specific  grounds for the dispute, and any supporting evidence the student wishes to be considered.  \(c\) The Director of Studies and Quality Assurance Office will acknowledge receipt of the dispute within five \(5\)  working days and will aim to resolve the matter within twenty-one \(21\) working days from the date of  acknowledgement.  \(d\) Where a re-marking or re-evaluation is requested and granted, the outcome of the re-assessment shall be  final and binding. A re-mark may result in the grade being upheld, increased, or decreased. \(e\) Disputes relating to administrative processing errors \(e.g. data entry mistakes\) will be resolved within five \(5\)  working days of submission.  \(f\) The Academy's determination of all academic disputes shall be final, subject only to any rights of appeal  provided under applicable Ugandan law. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
